    <div class="section-heading" style="margin-top: 40px;">Intrinsic safety installation check</div>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 60px;">
        <div class="main-content" style="flex: 2;">
            <p>If transmitters are operated in an intrinsically safe circuit, proof that the interconnection is intrinsically safe must be provided in accordance with EN/IEC 60079-0, EN/IEC 60079-11, EN/IEC 60079-14, EN/IEC 60079-17, EN/IEC 60079-28, EN/IEC 60079-29, EN/IEC 60079-34, EN/IEC 60079-36, EN/IEC 60079-49, EN/IEC 60079-51, EN/IEC 60079-52, EN/IEC 60079-53, EN/IEC 60079-54, EN/IEC 60079-55, EN/IEC 60079-56, EN/IEC 60079-60, EN/IEC 60079-61, EN/IEC 60079-62, EN/IEC 60079-63, EN/IEC 60079-64, EN/IEC 60079-65, EN/IEC 60079-66, EN/IEC 60079-67, EN/IEC 60079-68, EN/IEC 60079-69, EN/IEC 60079-70, EN/IEC 60079-71, EN/IEC 60079-72, EN/IEC 60079-73, EN/IEC 60079-74, EN/IEC 60079-75, EN/IEC 60079-76, EN/IEC 60079-77, EN/IEC 60079-78, EN/IEC 60079-79.</p>
            <p>In order to provide proof of intrinsic safety, the electrical limit value must be used as the basis for the Ex-type examination certificates for the equipment (devices); this includes the capacitance and inductance values of the cables.</p>
            <p>Proof of intrinsic safety is said to have been provided if the following conditions are fulfilled when a comparison is carried out in relation to the limit values of the equipment:</p>
            <div style="display: flex; gap: 60px; margin-top: 20px;">
                <div style="flex: 1;">
