    <h3 class="section-title">Additional information</h3>
    <p>In addition to the HART TAG, each device has a HART address. This address is set to 0 by default, which means that the device operates in HART standard communication mode (point-to-point operation).</p>

    <p>When an address in the range 1 to 15 is used, the device switches to the 'HART Multidrop' mode.</p>
    <p>This operating mode enables users to connect up to 15 devices to a power supply unit in parallel.</p>
    <p>In multidrop mode, an analog output signal that matches the process value is used exclusively for the power supply. In multidrop mode, sensor or process data information is available only as a HART signal.</p>
</div>

